# No Native Browser Dialogs

## Rule

**Never use `window.alert()`, `window.confirm()`, or `window.prompt()`** in any source file under version control. These native dialogs:

- Block the browser thread entirely
- Cannot be styled or themed
- Are inaccessible on some mobile browsers
- Break automated testing (Playwright, Cypress)
- Provide a poor, jarring UX

## Always Do This

When you need user confirmation before an action, use the `ConfirmModal` component from `src/components/lecturer/ConfirmModal.tsx`.

```typescript
import { ConfirmModal } from '../../components/lecturer/ConfirmModal';

// State to control the modal
const [confirmModal, setConfirmModal] = useState({
  open: false,
  title: '',
  description: '',
  variant: 'destructive' as 'default' | 'destructive',
  onConfirm: () => {},
});

// Open the modal instead of window.confirm()
setConfirmModal({
  open: true,
  title: t('common.areYouSure'),
  description: t('common.destructiveWarning'),
  variant: 'destructive',
  onConfirm: () => {
    // Your destructive action here
    void performDestructiveAction();
  },
});

// Render the modal
{confirmModal.open && (
  <ConfirmModal
    title={confirmModal.title}
    description={confirmModal.description}
    variant={confirmModal.variant}
    confirmLabel={t('common.confirm')}
    cancelLabel={t('common.cancel')}
    onConfirm={() => {
      confirmModal.onConfirm();
      setConfirmModal((prev) => ({ ...prev, open: false }));
    }}
    onClose={() =>
      setConfirmModal((prev) => ({ ...prev, open: false }))
    }
  />
)}
```

## Variant Guide

| Situation | Variant |
|---|---|
| Delete, deactivate, remove permanent data | `destructive` (red confirm button) |
| Replace leader, change assignment | `default` (blue confirm button) |
| Simple yes/no without risk | `default` |

## What to Do When You See `window.confirm()`

1. Replace it with a `ConfirmModal` state + open call
2. Move the destructive logic into the `onConfirm` callback
3. Remove the `window.confirm()` line entirely

## Pattern: Replacing `window.confirm()`

**Before (bad):**
```typescript
const ok = window.confirm('Delete this item? This cannot be undone.');
if (!ok) return;
await deleteItem();
```

**After (good):**
```typescript
const [confirmOpen, setConfirmOpen] = useState(false);

const handleDelete = () => {
  setConfirmOpen(true); // opens the modal instead of blocking
};

const confirmDelete = async () => {
  await deleteItem();
  setConfirmOpen(false);
};

// In JSX:
{confirmOpen && (
  <ConfirmModal
    title={t('common.areYouSure')}
    description={t('common.destructiveWarning')}
    variant="destructive"
    confirmLabel={t('common.delete')}
    cancelLabel={t('common.cancel')}
    onConfirm={confirmDelete}
    onClose={() => setConfirmOpen(false)}
  />
)}
```
